<div class="view"><section class="pg-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="crumb"><a href="/" data-portal="Home">Home</a> / Cancellation and Refund Policy</p><h1 class="pg-h1">Cancellation and Refund Policy</h1><p class="lead">How cancellation, rescheduling and refunds work for our Academy programmes, Studio projects and Originals products, with clear timelines.</p><p class="ld-meta"><span>Effective date: 12 November 2026</span><span>Last updated: 12 November 2026</span><span>Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited</span></p></div></section>
<section class="ld"><div class="wrap ld-grid">
<nav class="ld-toc" aria-label="On this page"><p class="ld-toc-h">On this page</p><ol><li><a href="#s1">Overview</a></li><li><a href="#s2">Academy programmes: cancellation by you</a></li><li><a href="#s3">Academy programmes: cancellation or change by us</a></li><li><a href="#s4">Studio projects and events</a></li><li><a href="#s5">Originals: games and tools</a></li><li><a href="#s6">What is not refundable</a></li><li><a href="#s7">How to request a cancellation or refund</a></li><li><a href="#s8">Disputes and chargebacks</a></li><li><a href="#s9">Changes to this Policy</a></li><li><a href="#s10">Contact</a></li></ol></nav>
<article class="ld-doc">

<div class="ld-sec" id="s1"><h2><span>1</span>Overview</h2><p>This Cancellation and Refund Policy explains how you can cancel, reschedule or seek a refund for services bought from Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited (“<b>Wizardlenz</b>”). It applies to Academy programmes, Studio projects and Originals products sold directly by us, and should be read with our <a href="/terms/">Terms and Conditions</a>. If your signed proposal, statement of work or programme confirmation contains different cancellation terms, those terms apply.</p><p>All refund periods are counted in calendar days before the scheduled start date (or event date) in your confirmation, and all amounts are in Indian Rupees (INR).</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s2"><h2><span>2</span>Academy programmes: cancellation by you</h2><p>Workshops, bootcamps, semester courses, faculty programmes and in-plant training in XR and AI require us to reserve trainers, equipment and schedules. Cancel by writing to <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a>. Refunds are calculated on the fees you have paid, as follows:</p><div class="ld-tw"><table class="ld-table"><thead><tr><th>Written notice received</th><th>Refund of fees paid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>15 days or more before the start date</td><td>100%, less any non-recoverable third-party costs already incurred (for example travel or venue bookings)</td></tr><tr><td>8 to 14 days before the start date</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>4 to 7 days before the start date</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>3 days or fewer before the start date, after the programme begins, or no-show</td><td>No refund</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>Rescheduling.</b> You may reschedule a confirmed programme once, free of charge, if you give at least 7 days’ written notice, subject to our trainer and equipment availability and to any travel costs already committed. Later or repeated changes are treated as a cancellation.</p><p><b>Participant substitution.</b> Where a programme is for named individuals, you may substitute another participant at no charge up to 48 hours before the start.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s3"><h2><span>3</span>Academy programmes: cancellation or change by us</h2><p>If we cancel a programme, are unable to deliver it for reasons within our control, or must postpone it for any reason, we will offer you a choice of (a) a new date, or (b) a full refund of the fees you paid for the cancelled programme. Programmes that rely on third-party AI platforms or accounts are delivered subject to those services’ availability; if a tool becomes unavailable we will provide a comparable alternative, and this alone is not a ground for refund. If a programme is interrupted midway for reasons beyond our control (for example illness of a trainer, power or venue failure or a government order), we will complete the remaining sessions on a rescheduled basis, or refund the fees for the undelivered portion pro rata. We are not liable for any other costs you incur.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s4"><h2><span>4</span>Studio projects and events</h2><p>Studio services are custom work, and fees are linked to milestones in the statement of work. Unless that document says otherwise:</p><ul><li><b>Before kick-off:</b> if you cancel in writing before work begins, we will refund the advance paid, less 10% (to cover proposal, planning and administrative effort) and any costs we have already committed.</li><li><b>After kick-off:</b> you pay for all milestones delivered and for work in progress on the current milestone, calculated by effort completed, plus non-cancellable third-party costs. The balance of any advance paid is refunded within the timeline in section 7.</li><li><b>Hardware, licences and third-party purchases:</b> equipment, software licences, assets and services bought specifically for your project are non-refundable once ordered.</li><li><b>VR event visualisation and live events:</b> cancellations within 14 days of the event date forfeit the fees for work already produced and any booked resources. The proposal sets out any further event-specific terms.</li><li><b>Defective deliverables:</b> if a deliverable does not materially meet the agreed specification, we will first correct it within a reasonable period. If we cannot do so, you may ask for a refund of the fees paid for that deliverable, which we will assess fairly and which will not exceed the amount paid for it.</li></ul></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s5"><h2><span>5</span>Originals: games and tools</h2><ul><li>Free products, including the ImmersiTest testing tool, have no price and so no refund.</li><li>Products purchased through third-party platforms such as itch.io are governed by that platform’s refund policy, and refund requests must be made to the platform.</li><li>For any paid product we sell directly, you may request a refund within 7 days of purchase if the product has a material defect that we cannot fix or does not work as described, provided you have not extensively used it. We may ask for details to help us diagnose the problem.</li></ul></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s6"><h2><span>6</span>What is not refundable</h2><ul><li>Fees for programmes already started or sessions already delivered, and fees for participants who do not attend.</li><li>Registration, booking or onboarding fees expressly stated as non-refundable at the time of payment.</li><li>Costs of third-party goods and services bought on your behalf and non-cancellable.</li><li>Certificates, course material or digital assets once delivered or downloaded, except where they are defective.</li><li>Payment-gateway or bank charges deducted by your payment provider, unless the cancellation is due to our fault.</li><li>Dissatisfaction that arises from circumstances outside our control, or from requirements that were not in the agreed scope.</li></ul></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s7"><h2><span>7</span>How to request a cancellation or refund</h2><ol class="ld-ol"><li>Email <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a> with the subject “Cancellation” or “Refund”, quoting your name, organisation, programme or project name, invoice or payment reference and the reason.</li><li>We will acknowledge your request within 3 business days.</li><li>We will review it and tell you the outcome and the refund amount within 7 business days of receiving all the information we need.</li><li>Approved refunds are paid to the original payment method (or the bank account the payment came from) within 7 to 10 business days of approval. Bank processing times may add a few days.</li></ol><p>Applicable GST is refunded in proportion to the fees refunded, and, where a tax invoice has been issued, we will raise a credit note as the law requires. Where payment was made through a payment gateway, refunds are processed through that gateway.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s8"><h2><span>8</span>Disputes and chargebacks</h2><p>Please contact us first so we can try to resolve any concern; most issues can be settled quickly. If you raise a chargeback or payment dispute without contacting us, we may suspend the related services while we respond, and any amount reversed will be set against the sums you owe us. Disputes that we cannot resolve together are handled as set out in the “Governing law and dispute resolution” section of our Terms and Conditions.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s9"><h2><span>9</span>Changes to this Policy</h2><p>We may update this Policy from time to time. The version on the Website on the date you confirm your booking applies to that booking. The “Last updated” date above shows the current version.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s10"><h2><span>10</span>Contact</h2><p>Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited. Registered office: Madurai, Tamil Nadu, India. Operations: Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India. Email: <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a>. We aim to respond to every query within 3 business days.</p></div>

<p class="ld-end">Questions about this document? Write to <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a>.</p>
</article></div></section></div>
